lar to the environment where we’ve got revenue slowing a little bit, but we’ve been targeting taking cost out of the business and that’s why we often say we don’t manage to the incremental margin, we’re managing the business for the long-term.","url":"https://huggingface.co/datasets/kurry/sp500_earnings_transcripts"},{"c":"ODFL 2019 Q2","e":"odfl","d":"2019-07-25","l":"tariffs","r":"analyst","s":"Jason Seidl","x":"In your non-industrial business were any of your customers talking about the tariffs impacting them in the first half of this year from a pull-forward perspective?","url":"https://huggingface.co/datasets/kurry/sp500_earnings_transcripts"},{"c":"ODFL 2019 Q2","e":"odfl","d":"2019-07-25","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Adam Satterfield","x":"We're independently trying to put on revenue at a good OR and always trying to take cost out of the business.","url":"https://huggingface.co/datasets/kurry/sp500_earnings_transcripts"},{"c":"ODFL 2019 Q2","e":"odfl","d":"2019-07-25","l":"cost_cuts","r":"analyst","s":"Allison Landry","x":"Do you think that your sort of over resource and you need to rightsize that a bit, and how should we think about that in the second half in terms of headcount levels and what impact that may have on productivity.","url":"https://huggingface.co/datasets/kurry/sp500_earnings_transcripts"},{"c":"ODFL 2019 Q4","e":"odfl","d":"2020-02-06","l":"tariffs","r":"management","s":"Adam Satterfield","x":"…costs for this year, probably somewhere around 4% on a per shipment basis and that becomes the baseline for the conversations that we have with our contractual customers and go -- will go into our thinking when we get to the point of announcing a GRI for our tariff-based business as well.","url":"https://huggingface.co/datasets/kurry/sp500_earnings_transcripts"},{"c":"ODFL 2020 Q1","e":"odfl","d":"2020-04-23","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"Adam Satterfield","x":"It's obviously been very supportive to us over the years to make sure that we're getting price increases to offset our cost inflation and to support the investments that frankly customers are demanding of us to continue to support technology investments and support capacity infrastructure as well.","url":"https://huggingface.co/datasets/kurry/sp500_earnings_transcripts"},{"c":"ODFL 2020 Q2","e":"odfl","d":"2020-07-30","l":"cost_cuts","r":"analyst","s":"Greg Gantt","x":"In addition, circumstances associated with the COVID-19 environment created certain cost savings that are expected to diminish in future periods, such as a reduction in group health and dental claims travel and customer entertainment.","url":"https://huggingface.co/datasets/kurry/sp500_earnings_transcripts"},{"c":"ODFL 2020 Q2","e":"odfl","d":"2020-07-30","l":"cost_cuts","r":"analyst","s":"Greg Gantt","x":"I mean certainly there will be some costs that will come back into the business and we'll be prepared for those, but there should be other cost savings opportunities.","url":"https://huggingface.co/datasets/kurry/sp500_earnings_transcripts"},{"c":"ODFL 2020 Q4","e":"odfl","d":"2021-02-04","l":"tariffs","r":"management","s":"Adam Satterfield","x":"We don't necessarily detail out, what our contractual business is done versus our tariff-related business.","url":"https://huggingface.co/datasets/kurry/sp500_earnings_transcripts"},{"c":"ODFL 2020 Q4","e":"odfl","d":"2021-02-04","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"Greg Gantt","x":"Once we really got the service click and lock it needed to be then we were in a much better position to raise our prices and I think we've been extremely disciplined over the years.","url":"https://huggingface.co/datasets/kurry/sp500_earnings_transcripts"},{"c":"ODFL 2021 Q1","e":"odfl","d":"2021-04-22","l":"tariffs","r":"management","s":"Adam Satterfield","x":"So when you've got that mix of business that has now shifted into a percentage of business rather than shifted into our 559 tariff base customers and our larger contractual customers, I think it just reflects the underlying demand for our customers businesses.","url":"https://huggingface.co/datasets/kurry/sp500_earnings_transcripts"},{"c":"ODFL 2021 Q1","e":"odfl","d":"2021-04-22","l":"tariffs","r":"management","s":"Adam Satterfield","x":"In recent months, our tariff based business is continuing to improve as a result and actually is trending slightly ahead as a percent of overall revenue than where we were pre pandemic.","url":"https://huggingface.co/datasets/kurry/sp500_earnings_transcripts"},{"c":"ODFL 2021 Q2","e":"odfl","d":"2021-07-28","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Adam Satterfield","x":"…at our own time performance and our claims ratio in regards to inventory management and so forth, and how maybe paying for a little bit more upfront for Old Dominion service can deliver cost savings if you think about things on a total cost of transportation standpoint for their customers.","url":"https://huggingface.co/datasets/kurry/sp500_earnings_transcripts"},{"c":"ODFL 2021 Q3","e":"odfl","d":"2021-10-28","l":"pricing_power","r":"analyst","s":"Jack Atkins","x":"How should we be thinking about maybe the core price increases in the LTL market more broadly?","url":"https://huggingface.co/datasets/kurry/sp500_earnings_transcripts"},{"c":"ODFL 2021 Q4","e":"odfl","d":"2022-02-02","l":"tariffs","r":"management","s":"Adam Satterfield","x":"Yes, Tom, we've kind of just stopped talking about contractual renewals, because I've somewhat feel like, that's, that's obviously a very big piece of the overall revenue equation, about 25% of our business is on our tariffs business, and certainly the majority being on contract.","url":"https://huggingface.co/datasets/kurry/sp500_earnings_transcripts"},{"c":"ODFL 2021 Q4","e":"odfl","d":"2022-02-02","l":"tariffs","r":"management","s":"Adam Satterfield","x":"We did the January numbers, I did mention this earlier, but we did take our general rate increase, which is on our tariffs business that was affected the beginning of January.","url":"https://huggingface.co/datasets/kurry/sp500_earnings_transcripts"},{"c":"ODFL 2021 Q4","e":"odfl","d":"2022-02-02","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"Adam Satterfield","x":"But, it all just sort of goes into it, whether it's price increases, other operational changes, that drive yields, and so forth, and the things that we look for, we'll say that, like I mentioned earlier.","url":"https://huggingface.co/datasets/kurry/sp500_earnings_transcripts"},{"c":"ODFL 2022 Q2","e":"odfl","d":"2022-07-27","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"Adam Satterfield","x":"And to improve the yield on an account, it's not always through a price increase either.","url":"https://huggingface.co/datasets/kurry/sp500_earnings_transcripts"},{"c":"ODFL 2022 Q2","e":"odfl","d":"2022-07-27","l":"pricing_power","r":"analyst","s":"Jordan Alliger","x":"And then just a follow-up on fuel and fuel surcharges, I know the mechanisms are supposed to work as a pass through.","url":"https://huggingface.co/datasets/kurry/sp500_earnings_transcripts"},{"c":"ODFL 2022 Q2","e":"odfl","d":"2022-07-27","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Adam Satterfield","x":"And it takes every employee coming in every day, thinking about what they can do to make this company better, whether it's improving our service and revenue opportunities or trying to take cost out of the equation as well.","url":"https://huggingface.co/datasets/kurry/sp500_earnings_transcripts"},{"c":"ODFL 2022 Q2","e":"odfl","d":"2022-07-27","l":"cost_cuts","r":"analyst","s":"Scott Group","x":"Do you see opportunities if tonnage stays negative to reduce headcount, or are you going to be potentially more reluctant to do that this time around just given the problems that everybody had hiring people?","url":"https://huggingface.co/datasets/kurry/sp500_earnings_transcripts"},{"c":"ODFL 2022 Q3","e":"odfl","d":"2022-10-26","l":"pricing_power","r":"analyst","s":"Amit Mehrotra","x":"…this is a pricing discipline question for the industry, which I ask every quarter, but I just want to get your perspective in terms of what you think the industry's ability to see yield ex-fuel positive pricing is next year based on everything you're seeing out there from a pricing perspective?","url":"https://huggingface.co/datasets/kurry/sp500_earnings_transcripts"},{"c":"ODFL 2022 Q3","e":"odfl","d":"2022-10-26","l":"cost_cuts","r":"analyst","s":"Greg Gantt","x":"So we're continuing to stay laser-focused on those kind of things and continue to try to drive some cost out when we can and where we can.","url":"https://huggingface.co/datasets/kurry/sp500_earnings_transcripts"},{"c":"ODFL 2022 Q4","e":"odfl","d":"2023-02-01","l":"pricing_power","r":"analyst","s":"Amit Mehrotra","x":"I guess what's surprising to me is some of the ones that have even a little bit weaker service that may be more tempted to lean into price have also announced big price increases.","url":"https://huggingface.co/datasets/kurry/sp500_earnings_transcripts"},{"c":"ODFL 2023 Q1","e":"odfl","d":"2023-04-26","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Marty Freeman","x":"We will also continue to work on improving the efficiency of our operations as we make our way through the balance of this year, which provides an opportunity to generate additional cost savings.","url":"https://huggingface.co/datasets/kurry/sp500_earnings_transcripts"},{"c":"ODFL 2023 Q1","e":"odfl","d":"2023-04-26","l":"cost_cuts","r":"analyst","s":"Chris Wetherbee","x":"Just want to get a sense maybe how much more room you have in terms of rightsizing that labor force?","url":"https://huggingface.co/datasets/kurry/sp500_earnings_transcripts"},{"c":"ODFL 2023 Q2","e":"odfl","d":"2023-07-26","l":"tariffs","r":"management","s":"Adam Satterfield","x":"I think some of that is, we are -- seems to be picking up some more of the smaller tariff-based customers that generally got a little bit lower weight per shipment.","url":"https://huggingface.co/datasets/kurry/sp500_earnings_transcripts"},{"c":"ODFL 2023 Q2","e":"odfl","d":"2023-07-26","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"Adam Satterfield","x":"And we talk about our cost inflation with customers and the need to have a price increase that it's 100 to 150 basis points above our cost inflation every year to support the significant investments that we're making in service center capacity and technologies.","url":"https://huggingface.co/datasets/kurry/sp500_earnings_transcripts"},{"c":"ODFL 2023 Q2","e":"odfl","d":"2023-07-26","l":"cost_cuts","r":"analyst","s":"Kevin Freeman","x":"And like Adam said, we'd look after our existing customers and we cost out every piece of business that comes through this truck line.","url":"https://huggingface.co/datasets/kurry/sp500_earnings_transcripts"},{"c":"ODFL 2023 Q2","e":"odfl","d":"2023-07-26","l":"cost_cuts","r":"analyst","s":"Ravi Shanker","x":"Did you take any short-term cost savings actions in this quarter that may potentially unwind if tonnage really comes back?","url":"https://huggingface.co/datasets/kurry/sp500_earnings_transcripts"},{"c":"ODFL 2023 Q4","e":"odfl","d":"2024-01-31","l":"pricing_power","r":"analyst","s":"Bascome Majors","x":"Based on the recent contract conversations, you said, certainly, your peers continue to raise price.","url":"https://huggingface.co/datasets/kurry/sp500_earnings_transcripts"},{"c":"ODFL 2024 Q3","e":"odfl","d":"2024-10-23","l":"pricing_power","r":"analyst","s":"Daniel Imbro","x":"…into the fourth quarter and then more broadly, if the macro remains this week, I guess do you expect to see any irrationality in the market that would make it harder for you guys to keep realizing price increases above inflation or how is your price realization going as you talk to customers?","url":"https://huggingface.co/datasets/kurry/sp500_earnings_transcripts"},{"c":"ODFL 2024 Q4","e":"odfl","d":"2025-02-05","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"Adam Satterfield","x":"We're still getting good price increases.","url":"https://huggingface.co/datasets/kurry/sp500_earnings_transcripts"},{"c":"ODFL 2025 Q1","e":"odfl","d":"2025-04-23","l":"tariffs","r":"management","s":"Adam Satterfield","x":"Some of that is probably going to be a tariff impact on parts and repairs.","url":"https://huggingface.co/datasets/kurry/sp500_earnings_transcripts"},{"c":"ODFL 2025 Q1","e":"odfl","d":"2025-04-23","l":"tariffs","r":"management","s":"Adam Satterfield","x":"And most of the feedback that we're getting from the field is customers are reporting uncertainty as it relates to tariffs.","url":"https://huggingface.co/datasets/kurry/sp500_earnings_transcripts"},{"c":"ODFL 2025 Q1","e":"odfl","d":"2025-04-23","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"Adam Satterfield","x":"And it could be looking at all the cost base data that we have and figuring out ways that we can help us save money, be more efficient with our customers that may help prevent as much of a price increase.","url":"https://huggingface.co/datasets/kurry/sp500_earnings_transcripts"},{"c":"ODFL 2025 Q1","e":"odfl","d":"2025-04-23","l":"pricing_power","r":"analyst","s":"Richa Harnain","x":"And then secondly, I think it's pretty impressive that you're continuing to get your price increases despite the competitive pricing environment across the freight market.","url":"https://huggingface.co/datasets/kurry/sp500_earnings_transcripts"},{"c":"ODFL 2025 Q2","e":"odfl","d":"2025-07-30","l":"tariffs","r":"management","s":"Adam Satterfield","x":"Anticipating that some of our part cost might be increasing due to the impact of tariffs and so forth.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2025/07/30/old-dominion-odfl-q2-2025-earnings-transcript/"},{"c":"ODFL 2025 Q2","e":"odfl","d":"2025-07-30","l":"tariffs","r":"management","s":"Adam Satterfield","x":"But then all the tariff conversation started, and then that just created more uncertainty that seemed to kind of throw cold water on what was developing at the time.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2025/07/30/old-dominion-odfl-q2-2025-earnings-transcript/"},{"c":"ODFL 2025 Q3","e":"odfl","d":"2025-10-29","l":"tariffs","r":"management","s":"Adam Satterfield","x":"And the impact of the tariff environment.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2025/10/29/old-dominion-odfl-q3-2025-earnings-transcript/"},{"c":"ODFL 2025 Q3","e":"odfl","d":"2025-10-29","l":"tariffs","r":"management","s":"Marty Freeman","x":"This is a general tariff for non-contract.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2025/10/29/old-dominion-odfl-q3-2025-earnings-transcript/"},{"c":"ODFL 2025 Q3","e":"odfl","d":"2025-10-29","l":"cost_cuts","r":"analyst","s":"Richa Harnane","x":"And really what stood out in this quarter was you controlling what you can control, again, that variable cost item and optimizing your workforce that helped you deliver a nice cost out for the quarter and a better OR than what we see as your normal sequential deterioration.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2025/10/29/old-dominion-odfl-q3-2025-earnings-transcript/"},{"c":"ODFL 2025 Q3","e":"odfl","d":"2025-10-29","l":"cost_cuts","r":"analyst","s":"Richa Harnane","x":"And then just also what prompted these cost savings now?","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2025/10/29/old-dominion-odfl-q3-2025-earnings-transcript/"},{"c":"ODFL 2025 Q4","e":"odfl","d":"2026-02-04","l":"ai_spend","r":"management","s":"Adam Satterfield","x":"We don't want to just say we're investing in you know, machine learning and AI just to be able to say it, where's the proof in the pudding?","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2026/02/04/old-dominion-odfl-q4-2025-earnings-transcript/"},{"c":"ODFL 2025 Q4","e":"odfl","d":"2026-02-04","l":"tariffs","r":"management","s":"Jeffrey Kauffman","x":"Some of the truckers I've been talking to said, listen, we're having trouble quoting our freight liners or our internationals because of the section two tariffs and people aren't certain what the rebates are gonna be.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2026/02/04/old-dominion-odfl-q4-2025-earnings-transcript/"},{"c":"ODFL 2025 Q4","e":"odfl","d":"2026-02-04","l":"tariffs","r":"management","s":"Jeffrey Kauffman","x":"I was just kind of curious what you're seeing on the equipment side in terms of quoting activity from the OEs in the wake of some of the tariff changes?","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2026/02/04/old-dominion-odfl-q4-2025-earnings-transcript/"},{"c":"ODFL 2025 Q4","e":"odfl","d":"2026-02-04","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Adam Satterfield","x":"But really pleased with our operations team as they've continued to try to right size the fleet and make sure we've got all the equipment the places we need, but also managing through our cost inflation from a repairs and maintenance standpoint.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2026/02/04/old-dominion-odfl-q4-2025-earnings-transcript/"},{"c":"ODFL 2025 Q4","e":"odfl","d":"2026-02-04","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Adam Satterfield","x":"And I think that's a reflection of the management team's efforts in that area and continuing to rightsize.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2026/02/04/old-dominion-odfl-q4-2025-earnings-transcript/"},{"c":"ODFL 2026 Q1","e":"odfl","d":"2026-04-29","l":"tariffs","r":"management","s":"Adam N. Satterfield","x":"We are pretty consistent with what we target for increases every year, be it with our general rate increase that applies to our tariff-based business—that is about 25% of our revenue overall—as well as what we try to achieve as we go through contract renewals.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2026/04/29/old-dominion-odfl-q1-2026-earnings-transcript/"},{"c":"ODFL 2026 Q2","e":"odfl","d":"2026-07-29","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"Adam N. Satterfield","x":"So, you know, we are we are not facing any purchase transportation challenges that maybe some of our competitors are and certainly not dealing with the cost inflation that go along with that dynamic with the truckload price increases.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2026/08/07/old-dominion-odfl-q2-2026-earnings-call-transcript/"},{"c":"ODFL 2026 Q3","e":"odfl","d":"2026-10-28","l":"ai_spend","r":"management","s":"Adam N. Satterfield","x":"From an overall data center and AI infrastructure build out, know, it is hard to put a number on it, but the size and scale of many of those facilities, I think a lot of that freight is maybe ending up on flat beds and some other sectors, but a lot of that freight is very high value and it is…","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2026/10/28/old-dominion-odfl-q3-2026-earnings-call-transcript/"}],"trends":{"theater":[[37,1,9797,0,0,0,5219,3892],[38,1,8443,0,0,0,3599,4205],[39,1,10852,0,0,0,6009,4182],[40,1,9801,0,0,0,5609,3571],[41,1,9968,0,0,0,5050,4268],[42,1,9930,0,0,0,4335,5015],[43,1,11591,0,0,0,6589,4450],[44,1,11180,0,0,0,7798,2716],[45,1,10288,0,0,0,3156,6476],[46,1,10606,0,0,0,3467,6698],[47,1,10755,0,0,0,5932,4395],[48,1,10319,0,0,0,7839,2037],[49,1,5916,0,0,0,2305,3225],[50,1,11515,0,0,0,6161,4893],[51,1,12764,0,0,0,8841,3563],[52,1,10697,0,0,0,5079,5189],[53,1,9783,0,0,0,6964,2523],[54,1,10042,0,0,0,6297,3370],[55,1,9849,0,0,0,7001,2439],[56,1,10296,0,0,0,7262,2585],[57,1,3671,0,0,0,1604,1660],[58,1,10402,0,0,0,6309,3654],[59,1,10997,0,0,0,1016,9489],[60,1,10052,0,0,0,6215,3339],[61,1,11418,0,0,0,8116,2870],[62,1,9385,0,0,0,6565,2160],[63,1,10487,0,0,0,7952,1628],[64,1,9719,0,0,0,6861,2068],[65,1,7866,0,0,0,4837,2172],[66,1,10087,0,0,0,7233,2239],[67,1,9376,0,0,0,5736,3165]],"cinema":[[37,1,9797,0,0,0,5219,3892],[38,1,8443,0,0,0,3599,4205],[39,1,10852,0,0,0,6009,4182],[40,1,9801,0,0,0,5609,3571],[41,1,9968,0,0,0,5050,4268],[42,1,9930,0,0,0,4335,5015],[43,1,11591,0,0,0,6589,4450],[44,1,11180,0,0,0,7798,2716],[45,1,10288